## 3. Commercial License Required

You must obtain a Commercial License from Vitruvian Systems LLC before you may
lawfully use the Software for Commercial Deployment, embedding, resale,
customer-facing deployment, hosted or managed service, or other commercial
product or service use if any of the following is true:

- you, together with your Affiliates, have Annual Gross Revenue of
  USD $1,000,000 or more; or
- you previously qualified for Small Entity Use but you, together with your
  Affiliates, have since reached or exceeded Annual Gross Revenue of
  USD $1,000,000.

If you exceed the USD $1,000,000 **Annual Gross Revenue threshold**, your rights
under Section 2 for Small Entity Use terminate immediately for that use unless
and until you obtain a Commercial License.

## 4. What To Do If You Cross The Annual Gross Revenue Threshold

If you or your corporate group, together with Affiliates, reach or exceed the
USD $1,000,000 Annual Gross Revenue threshold, you must do the following within
30 days:

1. email Vitruvian Systems LLC at emilio@vitruvian.systems;
2. identify your organization and intended continued commercial use; and
3. either obtain a Commercial License or stop the covered commercial use of the
   Software.

You must maintain reasonable records sufficient to show whether you remain
eligible for below-threshold commercial use and otherwise comply with this License.

If Vitruvian Systems LLC reasonably asks for confirmation of eligibility, an
authorized representative of your organization must provide a written
certification of compliance.

Upon reasonable written notice and a good-faith basis to believe that you may be
using the Software outside the scope of this License, Vitruvian Systems LLC may
request records reasonably necessary to verify your compliance with the revenue
threshold, Affiliate aggregation, and other eligibility conditions of this
License. You must provide such records within 15 business days.

Continued covered commercial use of the Software after loss of below-threshold
eligibility and without obtaining a Commercial License is unauthorized and
constitutes a material breach of this License. Vitruvian Systems LLC reserves
the right to seek appropriate license fees, injunctive relief, enforcement
costs, and any other remedies available at law or in equity, where permitted.

